{{ ref: ba7bdb2c-6ab9-422f-94fa-4369bf2de3e5 }}
```rust
pub trait Adapter {
  // stage 1: source text to syntax trees
  fn parse(&self, sources: &SourceSet) -> Result<SyntaxSet, AdapterError>;
  // stage 2: syntax trees to ir fragment with resolved edges
  fn bind(&self, syntax: SyntaxSet) -> Result<IrFragment, AdapterError>;
}
```
--{ ref: ba7bdb2c-6ab9-422f-94fa-4369bf2de3e5 }--

{{ ref: 9a8d92f8-a220-4a5b-9269-b00a34ebbac5 }}
- **Behaviour**: Dynamic constructs the binder cannot resolve statically (e.g. Python `getattr`) emit edges with `confidence` below 1.0 rather than being dropped. Parse failures raise `AdapterParseFailure`; structural resolution failures (broken workspace manifests) raise `AdapterBindFailure`. Re-export edges are emitted as-is — flattening happens during snapshot assembly in `engine`.
--{ ref: 9a8d92f8-a220-4a5b-9269-b00a34ebbac5 }--
{{ ref: 2bb77b46-92d8-459d-adaa-912709d43390 }}
- **Compatibility**: First release — no migration concerns. A fourth language is added by implementing the trait in a new crate; `core` is untouched by design (FR-2).
